;;; roster-not-observed.slatl — Motoi Scheme Reference · error-cards
;;; Census keys: not-a-pair, wrong-arity, division-by-zero, index-out-of-range,
;;;   program-too-big, frozen-sandbox, unquote-splicing-misplaced
;;; family: language (roster)   ·   census-status: roster-only-not-observed
;;; These keys EXIST in normalizeError's family roster, but Motoi does not
;;; currently throw a message that lands on them. Honest "reserved coordinate".

(dialect :applies ("motoi") :note "error-card — roster families with no observed throw yet")

(error-card :key "roster-not-observed"
  :name "Roster keys not yet observed"
  :family "language"
  :census-status "roster-only-not-observed"
  :library "error-cards"
  :training-eligible #t
  :confidentiality "public"
  :provenance "scheme/reference/error-cards/roster-not-observed.slatl"
  :status "real"

  :scheme-classification
"The normalizer (`lib/system/verb-stats.js`, `_ERR_FAMILIES`) reserves a family
regex for several classic error kinds. Reserving a coordinate is not the same as
occupying it: for the keys below, there is currently no code path in Motoi that
throws a message matching the regex — either the operation is a silent non-error
instead (see silent-non-errors), or it fires before the eval boundary (see
expand-and-reader-time), or the guarding feature is not wired. This card is the
honest ledger of that gap, so no reader mistakes a reserved key for a seen one."

  :trigger-code "(display (car 5))"
  :observed-output ""
  :normalizes-to "(none — car of a non-pair is a SILENT non-error, nothing thrown)"

  :meaning
"Each roster key below is a promise the taxonomy makes about a kind of failure it
COULD name. Today, probing Motoi for these produces either a silent wrong value or
a pre-eval error, so the census key stays at zero. Documenting that plainly is the
point: the census is a map, and this card marks the regions of the map that are
drawn but not yet visited. When a future change makes one of these throw cleanly
at the eval boundary, its count will start rising and this card's entry graduates
into a full card of its own."

  ;; The reserved coordinates, each with what Motoi does INSTEAD today (verified).
  :reserved-keys (
    (:key "not-a-pair"
     :regex "\\bexpected .*pair\\b | \\bnot a pair\\b"
     :probe "(display (car 5))"
     :today "SILENT — returns nothing, no throw. A strict Scheme would signal
'car: not a pair'. Motoi does not. So `not-a-pair` never fires; the closest
COUNTED sibling is the leaky not-a-procedure collision when a pair verb hits a
non-list of a different shape (e.g. (cdr 42) => a.slice is not a function)."
     :see "silent-non-errors, not-a-procedure")

    (:key "wrong-arity"
     :regex "\\bwrong (number of|arity)\\b"
     :probe "(display ((lambda (x y) x) 1))"
     :today "SILENT — missing argument is not checked; the lambda returns x and
ignores the absent y. Extra arguments are dropped the same way. Motoi does not
arity-check lambdas, so `wrong-arity` never fires."
     :see "silent-non-errors")

    (:key "division-by-zero"
     :regex "\\bdivision by zero\\b | \\bdivide by zero\\b"
     :probe "(display (/ 1 0))"
     :today "SILENT — yields +inf.0 (and (modulo 5 0) yields +nan.0). No error is
thrown, so `division-by-zero` never fires."
     :see "silent-non-errors")

    (:key "index-out-of-range"
     :regex "\\bindex out of (range|bounds)\\b"
     :probe "(display (vector-ref (vector 1) 8))"
     :today "SILENT — out-of-range vector read returns nothing, no throw. Note
some verbs DO report ranges in their own words (e.g. hash-table-ref: key not
found), but those land on misc-uncategorized, not this key."
     :see "silent-non-errors, misc-uncategorized")

    (:key "program-too-big"
     :regex "\\bprogram too big\\b"
     :probe "(not routinely triggerable from a one-liner)"
     :today "A sandbox SIZE guard. Reserved for when a submitted program exceeds
the size budget. Not observed from ordinary reference programs."
     :see "(sandbox limits)")

    (:key "frozen-sandbox"
     :regex "\\bfrozen sandbox\\b"
     :probe "(not triggerable without a frozen-sandbox policy in effect)"
     :today "A sandbox POLICY refusal. Reserved for a hardened execution mode.
Not observed in the open reference runtime."
     :see "(sandbox limits)")

    (:key "unquote-splicing-misplaced"
     :regex "\\bunquote-splicing not at top\\b"
     :probe "`,@x outside a quasiquote list position"
     :today "A quasiquote structural error. Reserved; when it fires it is
reader/expand-adjacent and may not reach the eval-boundary census."
     :see "expand-and-reader-time"))

  :how-to-detect
"Because these are mostly SILENT today, detection is the same discipline as the
silent-non-errors card: check preconditions yourself and raise your own error.
The following turns the silent `(car 5)` into a thrown, catchable failure:"
  :how-to-detect-code
"(define (safe-car x) (if (pair? x) (car x) (error \"car: not a pair\" x)))
(display (guard (e (#t (error-object-message e))) (safe-car 5)))"
  :how-to-detect-output "car: not a pair"

  :fix-shape
"For CODE today: do not rely on these keys firing — guard the preconditions
yourself (`pair?`, arity via explicit checks, `zero?` before divide, range before
`vector-ref`). For the LANGUAGE: wiring a clean Motoi-level throw for these
(instead of a silent coercion) is exactly the improvement that would move them
from 'reserved' to 'observed', and give the census real signal where it currently
has a blind spot."

  :lesson
"A taxonomy is honest only when it distinguishes categories it HAS SEEN from
categories it has merely NAMED. Several classic Scheme errors — not-a-pair,
wrong-arity, division-by-zero, index-out-of-range — have reserved census keys but
never fire in Motoi today, because the underlying operation silently returns a
wrong value instead of throwing. Naming that gap here prevents a reader (human or
model) from asserting 'Motoi throws division-by-zero' when it actually returns
+inf.0. The reserved keys are a to-do list for making the language stricter, not a
description of what it already does."

  :census-verbs (
    "(stats/error-count-of \"not-a-pair\")        ;; 0 today"
    "(stats/error-count-of \"wrong-arity\")       ;; 0 today"
    "(stats/error-count-of \"division-by-zero\")  ;; 0 today")

  :related-cards ("silent-non-errors" "not-a-procedure" "expand-and-reader-time" "misc-uncategorized"))
